VALUES (NULL, NULL, 216, 'Neverwinter Nights', 'Neverwinter Nights', 'game', 2002, 'https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co1t13.jpg', 'https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_1080p/yktl7hktq3uac7mlss54.jpg', 'Neverwinter Nights (NWN) is a third-person role-playing video game and is set in the fantasy world of the Forgotten Realms campaign setting, with the game mechanics based on the Dungeons & Dragons 3rd edition rules. The game engine was designed around an internet-based model for running a massively multiplayer online game (MMOG), which would allow end users to host game servers. The intent was to create a potentially infinite massively multiplayer game framework. This game was named after the original Neverwinter Nights online game; the first ever graphical massively multiplayer online role-playing game (MMORPG), which operated from 1991 to 1997 on AOL.', 'https://www.igdb.com/games/neverwinter-nights', '["Linux", "PC (Microsoft Windows)", "Mac"]', NULL, 7.7, 0, 1.01, '2026-11-26 23:52:17', '2026-11-26 23:52:17')
